            <div type="translation" source="bib:Kuppusamy+al2010_01">
                <p n="1">Hail! Prosperity!</p>
                
                <p n="1">27th year <supplied reason="subaudible">of the reign</supplied> of śrī-Kaṉṉara-tēvar.</p>
                
                <p n="1-3">The manner in which the great assembly, having met in the big hall of the Lord, have given in writing, after discussions and upon mutual agreement, is <supplied reason="subaudible">as follows</supplied>.</p>
                <p n="3-7">After purchase, I have given to this donation twenty units <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>ceṟu</foreign></supplied> from the property of Cempiyaṉ Muṉaippāṭi Mūvēntavēḷāṉ in Kaliyūṉṟi at Neriñci Kuṟumpaṟ Kaḻaṉi, our Brahmin settlement, for performing worship to the great Lord of śrī-Mūlastāṉam of our village through the Brahmins who are well versed in Vedas and to the person who supplies water from the Nelli Ēttam<note>That is, Ēṟṟam.</note> for the sacred bath.</p>
                <p n="7-8">We, the members of the great assembly have ratified this donation as long as the moon and the sun will last; we have made it tax-free.</p>
                <p n="8-10">Twenty-five <foreign>kaḻañcu</foreign>s of gold are to be collected in different ways from those who trespass this agreement, on behalf of the ruler of the day <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>aṉṟāḷ kō</foreign><note resp="part:emfr">The word <foreign>aṉṟāḷ</foreign> is not in the original text.</note></supplied>, as capital for the court of justice.</p>
                <p n="10-11">In this manner, we have given in writing, after discussions and upon mutual agreement, we the members of the great assembly.</p>
            </div>
            
